const _astro_dataLayerContent = [["Map",1,2,14,15,32,33,43,44,54,55,65,66,73,74,103,104,141,142,217,218,228,229],"authors",["Map",3,4],"team",{id:3,data:5,filePath:12,digest:13},{name:6,bio:7,social:8},"Southwell Media","A digital agency focused on building fast, beautiful, and accessible websites.",{twitter:9,github:10,linkedin:11},"https://twitter.com/southwellmedia","https://github.com/southwellmedia","https://linkedin.com/company/southwellmedia","src/content/authors/team.json","fc9436019dbd8ca6","blog",["Map",16,17],"en/welcome-to-velocity",{id:16,data:18,body:29,filePath:30,digest:31,deferredRender:27},{title:19,description:20,publishedAt:21,author:6,tags:22,draft:26,featured:27,locale:28},"Welcome to Velocity","Get started with Velocity, the modern Astro boilerplate with everything you need to build fast, beautiful websites.",["Date","2026-01-28T00:00:00.000Z"],[23,24,25],"astro","tutorial","getting-started",false,true,"en","# Welcome to Velocity\n\nVelocity is a production-ready starter template built on **Astro 6** and **Tailwind CSS v4**. It's designed to help you build fast, beautiful, and accessible websites with minimal setup time.\n\n## Features\n\n- 🚀 **Astro 6** - The latest version with all stable features\n- 🎨 **Tailwind CSS v4** - CSS-first design token system\n- 🌍 **Internationalization** - Built-in i18n with 3 languages\n- 🔍 **SEO Optimized** - Complete meta tags, OG images, and structured data\n- 🌙 **Dark Mode** - Automatic theme detection and toggle\n- ♿ **Accessible** - WCAG 2.2 AA compliant components\n\n## Getting Started\n\n1. Clone the repository\n2. Install dependencies with `pnpm install`\n3. Start the dev server with `pnpm dev`\n\nThat's it! You're ready to start building.\n\n## Customization\n\nVelocity is designed to be easily customizable. Start by editing:\n\n- `src/config/site.config.ts` - Site metadata\n- `src/styles/tokens/colors.css` - Brand colors\n- `src/i18n/translations/` - Translations\n\nHappy building! 🎉","src/content/blog/en/welcome-to-velocity.mdx","c85cd638bd780be7","blogs",["Map",34,35],"c2aump3t0xut5figfipkickx",{id:34,data:36},{title:37,content:38,publish_date:39,publishedAt:40,createdAt:41,updatedAt:42,locale:28},"Why Kiribati Communities Should Embrace Technology","Kiribati is made up of many islands spread across a vast ocean. That distance is part of what makes Kiribati unique — but it can also make daily life harder: information travels slowly, services are far away, and opportunities can feel limited. Technology won’t solve every challenge, but used wisely, it can help communities stay connected, strengthen livelihoods, and protect what matters most.\n\n### 1. Staying connected across islands\n\nFor families, churches, youth groups, and village leaders, communication is essential. Phones, messaging apps, and community internet points make it easier to share announcements, coordinate events, and check in on relatives. When transport is delayed or weather changes quickly, fast communication can make a real difference.\n\n### 2. Better access to education and skills\n\nOnline learning can support students and teachers with resources that may not be available locally — from learning materials to training for teachers and vocational skills for young people. Even a small computer lab or shared devices at a community center can open doors to new knowledge.\n\n### 3. Stronger local businesses and incomes\n\nTechnology helps small businesses reach customers, promote local products, and manage money more effectively. Fishers, farmers, and craftspeople can benefit from market information, digital payments, and simple tools for tracking sales and expenses.\n\n### 4. Health and public services closer to home\n\nTelehealth services, digital records, and better communication with clinics can reduce travel and waiting times. Communities can also use technology to share accurate public health information quickly, especially during emergencies.\n\n### 5. Preparing for climate impacts\n\nKiribati faces rising seas and changing weather. Technology can support early warnings, disaster coordination, and community awareness. It can also help document local conditions and share community voices with the wider world.\n\n### A balanced way forward\n\nEmbracing technology doesn’t mean leaving culture behind. It means choosing tools that fit local values: using i-Kiribati language content, teaching digital safety, and making sure elders, women, and youth can all participate. With smart choices and community leadership, technology can strengthen Kiribati — not replace it.",null,["Date","2026-06-09T12:47:34.723Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T12:47:33.225Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T12:47:34.714Z"],"events",["Map",45,46],"rt0phd33x7iltlljbaf2brfm",{id:45,data:47},{date:48,location:49,details:50,image:39,publishedAt:51,createdAt:52,updatedAt:53},["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"Teaoraereke, Tarawa","### Overview\n\nJoin us for an interactive **Leadership Workshop** designed to strengthen leadership fundamentals, align on our expectations for leaders, and practice the skills that drive high-performing, healthy teams. This session blends short concept briefings with hands-on exercises, peer discussion, and practical tools participants can apply immediately.\n\n### Who it’s for\n\n- People managers and team leads\n- Emerging leaders and high-potential individual contributors stepping into leadership responsibilities\n- Cross-functional project leads who influence without direct authority\n\n### Objectives (what participants will leave with)\n\nBy the end of the workshop, participants will be able to:\n\n- Clarify what “good leadership” looks like in our context (behaviors, standards, and decision principles)\n- Communicate with more structure and impact (especially in high-stakes or ambiguous situations)\n- Coach for growth using a repeatable framework (feedback, development plans, and accountability)\n- Improve delegation and ownership so work scales without losing quality\n- Navigate conflict and difficult conversations with confidence and empathy\n- Create clear goals and follow-through rituals that improve execution\n\n### Key topics\n\n- **Leading self first:** mindset, credibility, and values-based decision-making\n- **Communication & alignment:** setting direction, context-setting, and running effective 1:1s\n- **Coaching & feedback:** SBI/STAR feedback, feedforward, and growth conversations\n- **Delegation & accountability:** levels of ownership, decision rights, and follow-up loops\n- **Team dynamics:** psychological safety, inclusion, and managing conflict productively\n- **Execution leadership:** priorities, trade-offs, and building predictable delivery habits\n\n### Format\n\n- Short teaching segments (10–15 minutes each)\n- Small-group breakouts and role-play scenarios\n- Real-case problem solving (participants can bring a current leadership challenge)\n- Reflection prompts and personal action planning\n\n### Agenda (sample)\n\n1. **Welcome & goals** (10 min)\n2. **Leadership expectations & principles** (20 min)\n3. **Communication that scales** (30 min)\n4. **Break** (10 min)\n5. **Coaching + feedback practice** (45 min)\n6. **Delegation & accountability toolkit** (30 min)\n7. **Difficult conversations scenarios** (30 min)\n8. **Action plan + commitments** (15 min)\n9. **Wrap-up & next steps** (10 min)\n\n### What to prepare (recommended)\n\nBring:\n\n- One current leadership challenge (team, stakeholder, delivery, or interpersonal)\n- One conversation you’ve been avoiding or want to improve\n- A situation where you need to delegate more effectively\n\n### Expected outcomes\n\nAfter the workshop, participants will have:\n\n- A personal leadership action plan (2–3 commitments for the next 30 days)\n- Practical templates for 1:1s, feedback, and delegation check-ins\n- Increased clarity on how to lead meetings, projects, and teams with stronger alignment",["Date","2026-06-09T12:49:03.975Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T12:49:02.263Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T12:49:03.970Z"],"faqs",["Map",56,57],"general-en",{id:56,data:58,filePath:63,digest:64},{question:59,answer:60,category:61,order:62,locale:28},"What is Velocity?","Velocity is a production-ready starter template built on Astro 6 and Tailwind CSS v4. It includes everything you need to build fast, beautiful, and accessible websites.","general",1,"src/content/faqs/general-en.json","08d2e00ee7bc5e64","meta::meta",["Map",67,68,69,70,71,72],"astro-config-digest","{\"root\":{},\"srcDir\":{},\"publicDir\":{},\"outDir\":{},\"cacheDir\":{},\"site\":\"https://example.com\",\"compressHTML\":true,\"base\":\"/\",\"trailingSlash\":\"ignore\",\"output\":\"static\",\"scopedStyleStrategy\":\"attribute\",\"build\":{\"format\":\"directory\",\"client\":{},\"server\":{},\"assets\":\"_astro\",\"serverEntry\":\"entry.mjs\",\"redirects\":false,\"inlineStylesheets\":\"auto\",\"concurrency\":1},\"server\":{\"open\":false,\"host\":false,\"port\":4321,\"allowedHosts\":[]},\"redirects\":{},\"image\":{\"endpoint\":{\"entrypoint\":\"astro/assets/endpoint/node\",\"route\":\"/_image\"},\"service\":{\"entrypoint\":\"astro/assets/services/sharp\",\"config\":{}},\"dangerouslyProcessSVG\":false,\"domains\":[],\"remotePatterns\":[],\"layout\":\"constrained\",\"responsiveStyles\":false},\"devToolbar\":{\"enabled\":true},\"markdown\":{\"syntaxHighlight\":{\"type\":\"shiki\",\"excludeLangs\":[\"math\"]},\"shikiConfig\":{\"langs\":[],\"langAlias\":{},\"theme\":\"github-dark\",\"themes\":{},\"wrap\":true,\"transformers\":[]},\"remarkPlugins\":[],\"rehypePlugins\":[],\"remarkRehype\":{},\"processor\":{\"name\":\"unified\",\"options\":{\"remarkPlugins\":[],\"rehypePlugins\":[],\"remarkRehype\":{}}}},\"security\":{\"checkOrigin\":true,\"allowedDomains\":[],\"actionBodySizeLimit\":1048576,\"serverIslandBodySizeLimit\":1048576,\"csp\":false},\"env\":{\"schema\":{\"SITE_URL\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"STRAPI_URL\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"public\",\"default\":\"http://localhost:1337\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"STRAPI_TOKEN\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"secret\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"STRAPI_API_TOKEN\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"secret\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"EMAIL_API_KEY\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"secret\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID\":{\"context\":\"client\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"PUBLIC_GTM_ID\":{\"context\":\"client\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"CONTACT_FORM_ENDPOINT\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"secret\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"NEWSLETTER_API_KEY\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"secret\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"BING_SITE_VERIFICATION\":{\"context\":\"server\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"type\":\"string\"},\"PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\":{\"context\":\"client\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"default\":\"\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"PUBLIC_CONSENT_ENABLED\":{\"context\":\"client\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"default\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL\":{\"context\":\"client\",\"access\":\"public\",\"optional\":true,\"default\":\"\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"validateSecrets\":false},\"prerenderConflictBehavior\":\"warn\",\"fonts\":[{\"name\":\"Ubuntu\",\"cssVariable\":\"--font-ubuntu\",\"provider\":{\"name\":\"google\"},\"weights\":[400,500,700]},{\"name\":\"Inter\",\"cssVariable\":\"--font-inter\",\"provider\":{\"name\":\"google\"},\"weights\":[400,500,600,700]},{\"name\":\"Saira Condensed\",\"cssVariable\":\"--font-saira\",\"provider\":{\"name\":\"google\"},\"weights\":[500,600,700]}],\"experimental\":{\"advancedRouting\":false,\"clientPrerender\":false,\"contentIntellisense\":false,\"chromeDevtoolsWorkspace\":false,\"rustCompiler\":false,\"queuedRendering\":{\"enabled\":false}},\"legacy\":{\"collectionsBackwardsCompat\":false},\"session\":{\"driver\":{\"entrypoint\":\"unstorage/drivers/fs-lite\",\"config\":{\"base\":\"/Users/tibereritobakanaan/Projects/ekwebsite/frontend/node_modules/.astro/sessions\"}}}}","astro-version","6.4.5","content-config-digest","23a37381dceee928","partners",["Map",75,76,89,90],"o220wc21csar6qr8lqvwftpa",{id:75,data:77},{name:78,website_url:79,logo:39,projects:80,publishedAt:86,createdAt:87,updatedAt:88},"New Zealand High Commission","https://www.mfat.govt.nz/en/countries-and-regions/australia-and-pacific/kiribati/new-zealand-high-commission-to-kiribati",[81],{documentId:82,id:83,title:84,description:85},"uc3e9xrzazmp9eqydr07307u",7,"Community Empowerment","Working with CSO, Faith based organisations and local communities to build financial, digital and leadership skills.",["Date","2026-06-09T17:20:18.807Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:20:18.787Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:20:18.787Z"],"zwk1cpesltsgxaun8aa9crl1",{id:89,data:91},{name:92,website_url:93,logo:39,projects:94,publishedAt:100,createdAt:101,updatedAt:102},"US Embassy ","https://fj.usembassy.gov/",[95],{documentId:96,id:97,title:98,description:99},"eeff7lav2j0jdctt68wim7ue",9,"American Spaces","Implementing Youth Empowerment Program at the American Space situated in the Kiribati National Library",["Date","2026-06-09T17:19:39.678Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:19:39.662Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:19:39.662Z"],"pillars",["Map",105,106,114,115,123,124,132,133],"i73v6q4yee4t9iilchjs1l9o",{id:105,data:107},{title:108,slug:109,description:110,publishedAt:111,createdAt:112,updatedAt:113},"Building Partnership for Impact","building-partnership-for-impact","No single organization can meet the scale of challenges facing Kiribati alone — especially across a nation of scattered atolls where resources, services, and opportunities are unevenly distributed. We build partnerships that respect local leadership and bring together government, community groups, churches, schools, diaspora networks, and the private sector so that solutions are coordinated, culturally grounded, and practical to deliver.\n\nOur approach is to connect strengths: local knowledge and trusted relationships, technical expertise, funding, and delivery capacity. By aligning partners around shared goals and clear roles, we reduce duplication and ensure projects are designed with communities — not simply delivered to them. Strong partnerships also help ideas move from pilot to long-term programs, with the right support systems in place for maintenance, training, and continued learning.\n\nPartnerships are also how we grow impact beyond a single project. When we collaborate openly, share evidence, and invest in long-term relationships, we can unlock better services, stronger local organizations, and more resilient livelihoods — while ensuring benefits reach women, youth, and outer island communities.",["Date","2026-06-10T16:58:36.026Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:40:09.730Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:58:35.992Z"],"jvu7d9o8yktbmqa61cofz8rp",{id:114,data:116},{title:117,slug:118,description:119,publishedAt:120,createdAt:121,updatedAt:122},"Empowering Leaders & Communities","empowering-leaders-and-communities","We believe lasting change in Kiribati must be led locally — by people who understand the rhythms of island life, the realities of outer atolls, and the strengths already present in community networks. When leadership is rooted in culture and community priorities, solutions are more relevant, more trusted, and far more likely to endure beyond a single project or funding cycle.\n\nThat’s why we invest in building capability and leadership pathways: training, mentorship, and practical opportunities that help emerging leaders gain confidence, skills, and support. By strengthening local organizations, youth and women’s leadership, and community decision-making, we help communities move from being recipients of support to being designers and drivers of their own development.\n\nEmpowered communities are also better prepared to navigate climate pressures, economic uncertainty, and the rapid shift to digital services. When people have the knowledge, tools, and voice to advocate for themselves, they can protect what matters, take informed risks, and build inclusive opportunities for the next generation — on their own terms.",["Date","2026-06-10T16:58:40.210Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:40:09.719Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:58:40.205Z"],"x7rhva0e7wi1yqookpy7xi30",{id:123,data:125},{title:126,slug:127,description:128,publishedAt:129,createdAt:130,updatedAt:131},"Creating Conditions for Innovation","creating-conditions-for-innovation","Innovation in Kiribati isn’t only about new technology — it’s about creating the conditions where communities, local organizations, and young people can test ideas, learn quickly, and improve what already works. Across dispersed islands, solutions must be practical, low-cost, and adaptable to different atoll realities. We help turn local insights into workable pilots that can grow into sustainable programs.\n\nWe focus on the systems that make innovation possible: access to information, basic tools and infrastructure, skills training, and spaces where people can collaborate. That includes supporting community-led problem solving, strengthening local institutions to plan and deliver projects, and using evidence to guide decisions — not assumptions.\n\nBy building pathways from small experiments to wider adoption, we help communities move from “trying something once” to developing resilient, repeatable approaches. Over time, this creates a culture of learning and improvement that strengthens climate resilience, livelihoods, and services — even when resources are limited.",["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:12.401Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:12.390Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:12.390Z"],"zi89rq6eybjuburge7xicitz",{id:132,data:134},{title:135,slug:136,description:137,publishedAt:138,createdAt:139,updatedAt:140},"Enabling Digital Participation","enabling-digital-participation","As services, education, and economic opportunities increasingly move online, digital inclusion becomes a matter of fairness and resilience. We work to ensure I-Kiribati communities — including women, youth, and outer island residents — can participate safely and confidently in the digital world, not be left behind by connectivity gaps or low digital literacy.\n\nOur work supports practical access and capability: foundational digital skills, trusted information, and tools that help people use digital services for real needs — applying for opportunities, accessing learning, managing finances, and staying connected to networks and support.\n\nWe also prioritize digital trust and safety. Communities need to understand online risks, protect personal information, and navigate misinformation. By strengthening digital confidence and responsibility, we help people use technology as an enabler of opportunity — expanding education, improving livelihoods, and supporting stronger community connections across every atoll.",["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:38.528Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:38.524Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:07:38.524Z"],"projects",["Map",96,143,82,204],{id:96,data:144},{title:98,slug:145,description:99,image:146,project_status:185,objectives:186,location:187,metrics:188,partners:189,pillars:192,testimonials:194,publishedAt:201,createdAt:202,updatedAt:203,locale:28},"american-spaces",{url:147,alternativeText:39,width:148,height:149,formats:150},"/uploads/Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f.jpeg",4080,3072,{thumbnail:151,small:161,large:169,medium:177},{name:152,hash:153,ext:154,mime:155,path:39,width:156,height:157,size:158,sizeInBytes:159,url:160},"thumbnail_WhatsApp Image 2026-06-10 at 13.42.13.jpeg","thumbnail_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f",".jpeg","image/jpeg",207,156,9.73,9732,"/uploads/thumbnail_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f.jpeg",{name:162,hash:163,ext:154,mime:155,path:39,width:164,height:165,size:166,sizeInBytes:167,url:168},"small_WhatsApp Image 2026-06-10 at 13.42.13.jpeg","small_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f",500,376,45.29,45291,"/uploads/small_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f.jpeg",{name:170,hash:171,ext:154,mime:155,path:39,width:172,height:173,size:174,sizeInBytes:175,url:176},"large_WhatsApp Image 2026-06-10 at 13.42.13.jpeg","large_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f",1000,753,154.97,154974,"/uploads/large_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f.jpeg",{name:178,hash:179,ext:154,mime:155,path:39,width:180,height:181,size:182,sizeInBytes:183,url:184},"medium_WhatsApp Image 2026-06-10 at 13.42.13.jpeg","medium_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f",750,565,91.53,91534,"/uploads/medium_Whats_App_Image_2026_06_10_at_13_42_13_a55535050f.jpeg","completed","Our core mission is to host engaging workshops that connect local youth with the modern digital world. As internet use rapidly grows across Kiribati, we focus on helping high school students and young adults build essential skills for their future. Through these programs, we empower participants by strengthening their abilities in leadership, career planning, financial literacy, and online safety.","South Tarawa","### Overall Reach\n- Total Participants: 714 Youth  \n- Age Demographics: 86.4% of participants were aged 14–25  \n- Gender Breakdown: 64% Female (456 participants) | 36% Male (255 participants) | <1% Unidentified  \n- Total Workshops Delivered: 24 workshops spanning 16 themed topics  \n\n### Workshop Delivery by Theme\n- Leadership: 5 workshops (21%) | 153 participants  \n- Financial Literacy: 4 workshops (17%) | 178 participants  \n- Cyber Security: 4 workshops (17%) | 142 participants  \n- Career Building: 4 workshops (17%) | 76 participants  \n- Citizenship: 3 workshops (12%) | 96 participants  \n- Professional Development: 3 workshops (12%) | 69 participants  \n\n### \nLearning Impact (Confidence & Understanding)\n- CV Confidence: Prior to the presentation, the majority of students reported \"some\" or \"a little\" confidence; after the presentation, the metric shifted heavily toward students feeling \"mostly\" or \"very\" confident.  \n- Career Confidence: Prioritized before/after data shows a substantial increase in students moving into the \"mostly\" and \"very\" confident tiers regarding their future career planning.  \n- Digital Respect & Smart Internet Use: Post-workshop data shows a definitive positive shift toward higher levels of student understanding and smart digital practices.",[190],{documentId:89,id:191,name:92},2,[193],{documentId:123,id:191,title:126},[195],{documentId:196,id:197,quote:198,author:199,role:200},"ifqx24m187iperq754vibb63",3,"Empower Kiribati program is an eye-opener to our community.","Mary John","Community Leader",["Date","2026-06-11T17:29:05.685Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:20:58.798Z"],["Date","2026-06-11T17:29:05.677Z"],{id:82,data:205},{title:84,slug:206,description:85,image:39,project_status:39,objectives:39,location:39,metrics:39,partners:207,pillars:210,testimonials:213,publishedAt:214,createdAt:215,updatedAt:216,locale:28},"community-empowerment",[208],{documentId:75,id:209,name:78},4,[211,212],{documentId:132,id:209,title:135},{documentId:123,id:191,title:126},[],["Date","2026-06-10T16:33:11.941Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T17:21:44.736Z"],["Date","2026-06-10T16:33:11.934Z"],"resources",["Map",219,220],"s26pw18g5nrifb4dmlia4vj2",{id:219,data:221},{title:222,description:223,content_blocks:224,publishedAt:225,createdAt:226,updatedAt:227,locale:28},"Top tips for parents","Parents guide on how to protect your child online.",[],["Date","2026-06-09T14:23:26.837Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T14:23:26.827Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T14:23:26.827Z"],"testimonials",["Map",196,230],{id:196,data:231},{quote:198,author:199,role:200,image:39,publishedAt:232,createdAt:233,updatedAt:234},["Date","2026-06-11T16:59:37.464Z"],["Date","2026-06-09T18:18:18.016Z"],["Date","2026-06-11T16:59:37.409Z"]];

